      "local_entries": ["agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/App.tsx","agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/features/navigation/desktopProductionRouteRegistry.ts","agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/features/navigation/desktopProductionRouteRuntime.ts","agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/features/tenant/tenantAnalyticsRouteModule.tsx","agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/features/tenant/TenantAnalyticsPage.tsx","agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/features/tenant/tenantAnalyticsController.ts","agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/plugins/desktopTenantAnalyticsAuthorityModuleV2.ts","agi-stack/apps/desktop/src/plugins/desktopTenantAnalyticsContractV2.ts","agi-stack/apps/desktop/sidecar/src/local_runtime/parity_routes.rs","agi-stack/apps/desktop/sidecar/src/local_runtime/parity_routes/tenant_analytics.rs"],
      "judgment_rationale": "Cloud Desktop mounts a native tenant-scoped analytics route and strictly consumes the Web analytics contract for 7-day, 30-day and 90-day periods. The shared controller covers loading, empty, ready, degraded, conflict, forbidden, unavailable, retry and scope-switch states without remounting the active workbench. Local Desktop exposes the same native route through a sidecar authority: the project total and project identities are authoritative, while memory and storage aggregates remain field-level unavailable rather than being fabricated as zero."
